            '<h2>The operational angle</h2>',
            '<p>Serverless and connection-pooled Postgres offerings have removed much of the old operational pain, including the connection-limit problem that made Postgres awkward with serverless functions. Check whether your host provides pooling or an HTTP driver, because a serverless app opening a raw connection per invocation will exhaust the pool under load. This trips up more teams than any query-performance issue.</p>',
            '<h2>Verdict</h2>',
            '<p>For a typical SaaS backend in 2026, Postgres is the sensible default: it covers relational and document workloads, the tooling is mature, and the flexibility argument that once favoured document stores is largely answered by JSONB. Choose a document database when your data is genuinely document-shaped or your team is materially more productive in it — both legitimate reasons, and both worth stating explicitly rather than assuming.</p>',
